<header><p class="st-kicker">imperial city · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Free Imperial City of Rothenburg</h1><p class="st-meta">1274 CE – 1803 CE · capital Rothenburg ob der Tauber</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Franconian imperial city above the Tauber whose medieval walls and streets survived almost intact, made famous by the legend of the Master Draught.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rothenburg-ob-der-tauber">Rothenburg</a> grew below a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a> castle on a spur above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tauber">Tauber</a> valley in the 12th century. After the fall of the Hohenstaufen, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-i-of-germany">King Rudolf I</a> confirmed its status as an imperial city in 1274, and it soon threw off the last rights of outside lords.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A patrician council ruled. Under the mayor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heinrich-toppler">Heinrich Toppler</a>, who died in prison in 1408 after the city fell foul of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rupert-of-germany">King Rupert</a>, the city built up one of the largest rural territories of any imperial city. It lived from farming, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and wool. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rothenburg-ob-der-tauber">Rothenburg</a> adopted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> in 1544. In 1631 it was taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johann-tserclaes-count-of-tilly">Tilly</a>'s imperial army, an episode remembered in the legend of the Master Draught.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Impoverished by war, the city stagnated, which preserved its medieval appearance. It lost its freedom to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> in 1802 to 1803 and became a celebrated tourist destination; its old town was carefully restored after damage in 1945.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/free-imperial-city-of-rothenburg.jpg" alt="Free Imperial City of Rothenburg" width="320" height="214"><figcaption>Image: Berthold Werner · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rothenburg_BW_4.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1274 CE – 1803 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>imperial city</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Rothenburg ob der Tauber</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Heinrich Toppler</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>East Franconian German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Rothenburg ob der Tauber</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1538&amp;focus=free-imperial-city-of-rothenburg" aria-label="Free Imperial City of Rothenburg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4914 457 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Free Imperial City of Rothenburg lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5234 713L5229 694M5234 713L5269 749"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5229 694h0M5269 749h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5234 713h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5234 713h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1538&amp;focus=free-imperial-city-of-rothenburg">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
